# Studio architecture — decisions already made

Full reasoning lives in `docs/architecture.md` (or wherever `music_player_architecture_plan.md`
was committed) — read that if you need the "why." This file is the condensed "what," so you
don't have to re-derive it or suggest an alternative stack.

## Stack — don't propose swapping these without being asked

| Concern | Library | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Audio engine | `media_kit` (libmpv-backed) | gapless, broad format support, exposes low-level mpv property/filter access for EQ/ReplayGain |
| State management | Riverpod | |
| Local database | `drift` over `sqlite3` | reactive queries — UI subscribes directly to e.g. "tracks in this album" |
| Dynamic color | `palette_generator` + `material_color_utilities` | seed color → tonal palette, same pipeline for auto (from art) and custom (user hue) — see design-system rule |
| Dockable layout | `docking` | VS Code–style resizable/drag panels |
| Frameless window | `bitsdojo_window` or `window_manager` | fully custom titlebar, no native chrome |
| Tray / hotkeys | `tray_manager`, `hotkey_manager` | OS media keys, tray mini-controls |
| Tag I/O | pure-Dart tag lib for now; `lofty` (Rust) via `flutter_rust_bridge` only if that's outgrown | don't reach for the Rust bridge prematurely |

## Repo layout — put new code in the matching folder

```
lib/
  playback/       # media_kit wrapper, queue, gapless, visualizer tap
  playback/dsp/   # ReplayGain, equalizer (mpv af/filter passthrough), crossfade engine
  library/        # scanner, tag I/O, Drift schema + queries
  lyrics/         # LRCLIB client, .lrc parsing/cache, sync timing
  providers/      # LocalFileProvider, SpotifyMetadataProvider, resolver — pluggable interface
  theming/        # skin definitions, palette pipeline (auto + custom seed), ThemeExtensions
  ui/
    layout/           # docking panel setup, custom titlebar
    now_playing/
    library_browser/
    lyrics/
    visualizer/
    settings/         # appearance, playback & sound (EQ/ReplayGain/crossfade)
  state/          # Riverpod providers tying it together
```

This is feature-first: a feature's data/domain/UI live together under its own folder rather than
split across global `models/`, `screens/`, `widgets/` buckets.

## The one architectural rule that matters most

**The Playback Core only ever talks to a URI — it never branches on "is this local or
Spotify."** `LocalFileProvider` and `SpotifyMetadataProvider` (+ its audio resolver) both resolve
down to a playable URI before `media_kit` ever sees them. Don't add `if (source == local)`
branching inside playback, theming, or the visualizer — that logic belongs entirely in the
provider layer. This is the split that makes the later streaming linkup a bolt-on instead of a
rewrite (same pattern as the open-source Spotube app).

## Advanced audio features — effort/approach per feature

- **ReplayGain** — mostly wiring: mpv has native support, expose Track/Album/Off in settings and
  pass through. Test against real library tags; mpv's fallback-gain behavior has known quirks.
- **Equalizer** — UI + settings only with media_kit_libs_audio. That libmpv has no
  `firequalizer` or `aresample`; writing `af=lavfi=[...]` mutes playback and flushes
  the decoder (playhead jumps). Do not send a graphic EQ graph to mpv.
- **Crossfade — real engineering, not a config flag.** libmpv plays one stream at a time. Real
  crossfade means two concurrent `media_kit` `Player` instances: pre-load the next track, ramp
  its volume up while ramping the outgoing player down over the crossfade duration, then swap
  which instance is "active." Treat as its own mini-project, same tier of effort as the real FFT
  visualizer — don't scope it into a routine feature PR.
- **Lyrics** — [LRCLIB](https://www.lrclib.net/), free/no-key. Look up by artist/title/duration,
  cache synced `.lrc` (fall back to plain text) alongside the library index, parse timestamps
  client-side for the current-line-centered scrolling view.

## Visualizer — phase it, don't attempt real FFT first

v1: amplitude-envelope reactive visuals driven off playback position/level (easy, still looks
good). v2 (later phase): true PCM/spectrum tap — flagged as the hardest technical piece in the
whole app; budget it as its own project, not a routine task.

## Phased roadmap (for prioritizing what "done" means at any point)

1. **Core player, local only** — folder scan + Drift index, `media_kit` playback + queue, basic
   unskinned UI, frameless window shell.
2. **Look and feel** — full theming/skin engine, dynamic-color pipeline (auto + custom seed),
   `docking` layout, visualizer v1.
3. **Sound quality and lyrics** — ReplayGain, equalizer, LRCLIB lyrics.
4. **Streaming linkup** — Spotify metadata provider + swappable audio resolver behind the
   provider interface.
5. **Depth** — real FFT visualizer, dual-player crossfade engine, skin/plugin marketplace format.

If asked to build something from a later phase before an earlier one is solid, flag that rather
than silently doing it out of order.
